 "final_message": "I've made all twelve changes, and the test suite passes with 6 tests: the 4 existing ones plus the 2 new ones. I didn't add tests for the other fixes, so those were only checked by the existing suite.\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** `conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate`, `conversions_in_window`, `parse_session_log`, `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts` and `campaign_summary` now follow SPEC sections 1\u20137. For example, the `converted` field now maps `1`, `0` and empty to True, False and None, and blank and `#` lines are skipped. Errors name the 1-based line number, counting skipped lines.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added a test that `None` counts as not converted, and a test that `dedupe_sessions` keeps the last of several sessions with the same id.\n- **Item 11:** The README entry for `conversions_in_window` now says it sums the last `days` entries. I also added an entry for `daily_conversion_counts`.\n- **Item 12:** Checking the rest of the package turned up three more bugs, which I fixed:\n  - `top_converting_groups` now excludes empty groups, breaks ties by ascending group name, and returns an empty list for a negative `n`.\n  - `conversion_rate_by_group` now maps empty groups to `None` and sorts its keys.\n  - `longest_flag_streak` never reset its running count, so it counted non-consecutive days. It now resets on any day that isn't above 0.\n\nOne choice goes beyond the spec. A `converted` value other than `1`, `0` or empty raises `ValueError` with the line number, because the spec doesn't say what to do with it.",
